```

### Minimal Render Function
```javascript
const seenIds = new Set();
function addMessage(msg) {
  if (seenIds.has(msg.id)) return;
  seenIds.add(msg.id);
  const el = document.createElement('div');
  el.textContent = msg.text;
  document.getElementById('chat').appendChild(el);
}
```

## Concept Overview
Dynamic programming optimizes recursive problems by caching subproblem results. In React, useMemo prevents expensive recalculations during re-renders.

## Implementation Details
### Top-Down Memoization (Recursive)
```javascript
const fibonacci = useMemo(() => {
  const memo = {};
  const fib = (n) => {
    if (n in memo) return memo[n];
    if (n <= 1) return n;
    memo[n] = fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);
    return memo[n];
  };
  return fib;
}, []);
```

### Bottom-Up Tabulation (Iterative)
```javascript
const fibonacci = useMemo(() => {
  return (n) => {
    if (n <= 1) return n;
    let prev = 0, curr = 1;
    for (let i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
      [prev, curr] = [curr, prev + curr];
    }
    return curr;
  };
}, []);
```

## Common Pitfalls
- **Dependency array**: Empty array [] ensures function isn't recreated
- **Memory leaks**: Large memo objects can cause memory issues
- **Over-optimization**: useMemo overhead may exceed benefits for simple calculations
- **Referential equality**: useMemo preserves function reference for child components

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests real-world patterns: per-field state via closures, per-field debouncing, cancellation of outdated requests with AbortController, and a global concurrency limiter to prevent overload, plus mapping responses to correct field.

## Key Concepts

- Closures for per-field state
- Debounce patterns
- AbortController cancellation
- Concurrency limit with a simple semaphore
- Mapping async results to UI per-field

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal concurrency-limited debounced fetch per field using closures
function createFieldController(fetchUrl, maxConcurrent = 4) {
  let debounceTimer;
  let abortController;

  return {
    onInput: async (term) => {
      // Cancel previous request
      if (abortController) {
        abortController.abort();
      }

      // Clear existing debounce
      clearTimeout(debounceTimer);

      // Set new debounce
      debounceTimer = setTimeout(async () => {
        // Check global concurrency limit
        if (globalInFlight >= maxConcurrent) {
          await waitForSlot();
        }

        globalInFlight++;
        abortController = new AbortController();

        try {
          const response = await fetch(`${fetchUrl}?q=${term}`, {
            signal: abortController.signal
          });

          if (!abortController.signal.aborted) {
            const suggestions = await response.json();
            updateFieldUI(suggestions);
          }
        } catch (error) {
          if (error.name !== 'AbortError') {
            console.error('Fetch error:', error);
          }
        } finally {
          globalInFlight--;
        }
      }, 300);
    }
  };
}
```

